{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8Me2hv65hReVTCCfmbc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything, because this request conflicts with a recorded team policy.\n\nPlexus memory has a fact from builder-1: \"emails in a task title are replaced with the literal `[email]` before storing (compliance C2)\". That's the redaction in commit a6fcc0e. Storing titles exactly as typed would remove that protection. So `jane.doe@acme.example` would be written to storage in plain text.\n\nSupport's need is real: on-call people need to know who to contact. But a compliance rule is not mine to override on a support request alone. These are some ways to resolve it:\n\n1. **Compliance approves an exception.** If whoever owns C2 signs off, I'll remove the redaction from `add`, add the test, run the suite and commit. I'd also update the Plexus fact so the policy record stays accurate.\n2. **Put the contact in a separate field.** For example, add `--contact jane.doe@acme.example`, stored apart from the title and handled under whatever rules compliance sets for it. The title stays redacted.\n3. **Use a customer ID or name in the title.** For example, \"Call Jane Doe (acct 4821) about the renewal\". It carries no email, so no policy change is needed.\n\nWhich should I do? If compliance has already approved option 1, tell me who approved it and I'll go ahead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":20747,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":977},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0aeb69a-74ec-4e39-a7c2-c652e4d89a19","uuid":"1cb0bdea-9190-4610-b5ae-51bfd831e560","timestamp":